{
  "summary": "This experiment tested an image-only model using ResNet50, achieving validation accuracy of 0.2079 and F1 score of 0.1718, which underperforms both the multimodal baseline (0.5266 accuracy) and the RNA-only baseline (0.4849 accuracy). The result suggests image data alone may not be sufficient for this task, but uncertainty remains about the relative effectiveness of single-modality approaches due to differing encoder configurations (ResNet50 vs. PCA) and lack of direct comparison between image-only and RNA-only models with equivalent encoding methods."
}

